  "reviewed_on": "2026-07-30",
  "summary": "Episode 77 is framed as locker-room talk while Asa Akira is absent, then repeatedly turns absent partners, fans and workers into intimate material without demonstrated publication consent. Its strongest documentary value is not the explicit detail but the participants' live recognition that boundaries are being crossed: a private partner is said not to want her medical and sexual life discussed; the room says the show has become large enough to affect real encounters; and a bowling bet is treated as if it could transfer access to an absent co-host's body. The archive minimizes those dossiers and rejects sex-for-shelter advice, violence, wager-based consent, secret-recording exceptionalism, rape misinformation, sex-worker stigma and unpaid-restaurant-work advice. Public material remains rich: Choe's November 20, 2013 alice + olivia collaboration with Stacey Bendet; Sushi Nakazawa, David Chang, Aziz Ansari and Toro; Dark Dick's episode-specific fan art; the DVDASA hiring experiment; Choe's claimed 8MM set graffiti; and the 500-copy Into the Limelight vinyl with Edison and Capsule Labs credits. Named dialogue remains withheld.",
  "speaker_policy": "Named dialogue remains withheld. Episode 77 has zero diarized turns and five coarse window embeddings for a changing ensemble. Public participants are contextually known, but no independently held-out multispeaker validation has passed.",
  "sensitivity": "Absent-person sexual disclosure; coercive shelter recap; choking; fan harassment; workplace status and role stacking; drug speculation; unpaid labor; private proposal logistics; private medical information; explicit publication objection; body shaming; mental-health speculation; secret intimate recording; rape misinformation; bodily fluids; disordered eating; sex-worker stigma; wager-based sexual entitlement; workplace sexualization; fan violence.",
